codex
The full reduction confirms a hard cap issue: its stack has `31ℓ+98k` pancakes and every certified tight path has `16ℓ+50k` flips. Under the 256-atom output limit, reduction images can encode only a handful of effective variables, so they cannot carry the paper’s NP-hard regime. I’m therefore testing a native inverse-generated family of bounded pancake routes against breakpoint IDA*: unrestricted greedy sorting is explicitly kept below the allowed flip budget so it cannot serve as a shortcut.
