codex
The cap-bound concern is now resolved narrowly: there is a valid shipping window at 240 flips. In the exact tight regime, 32–2,048-wide beam searches, four natural greedy rules, random efficient walks, and an optimized exhaustive DFS all failed on the tested high-density instances. I’m replacing the earlier slack/neutral draft with this theorem-aligned construction and making the random-guess test follow efficient branches rather than sample implausible flip noise.
