Implemented the native, breakpoint-tight pancake-flipping generator based on [Theorems 18–19 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1111.0434v2).

Files:

- [gen_1111_0434.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.0434/gen_1111_0434.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.0434/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.0434/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.0434/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.0434/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.0434/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: each 0/8.
- Standard exhaustive search: 0/8 after 2,000,000 total nodes.
- Shipping answer: 240 elements, 1,114 characters, 481 lexical tokens.
- Doubled-size construction still verifies.

The only blocker is STEP 4: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, hinted, and placebo redraw. The script-owned error transcripts are preserved, but there is no valid oracle verdict, so the result is not yet submission-ready.
